  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「セイヨウハナズオウ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%BB%E3%82%A4%E3%83%A8%E3%82%A6%E3%83%8F%E3%83%8A%E3%82%BA%E3%82%AA%E3%82%A6",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 109211595,
      "text": "セイヨウハナズオウ は、マメ科ハナズオウ亜科の落葉灌木で、南欧から西南アジアにかけて自生する。春に濃い桃色の花をたくさんつける。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cercis siliquastrum」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cercis_siliquastrum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1360419475,
      "text": "Cercis siliquastrum, commonly known as European Cercis, the Judas tree or Judas-tree, is a small deciduous species of redbud in the flowering plant family Fabaceae which is noted for its prolific display of deep pink flowers in spring. It is native to Southern Europe and Western Asia."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "ja": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「セイヨウハナズオウ」の節「栽培」",
        "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%BB%E3%82%A4%E3%83%A8%E3%82%A6%E3%83%8F%E3%83%8A%E3%82%BA%E3%82%AA%E3%82%A6#%E6%A0%BD%E5%9F%B9",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 109211595,
        "heading": "栽培",
        "text": "セイヨウハナズオウは、肥沃で水捌けのよい、深い土壌を好み、満面の日光か、もしくは部分的な日蔭を好む。日照りにも耐性がある。\n栽培品種に次のようなものがある。\n\nアルバ 'Alba' - 白花\nボドナン 'Bodnant' - 赤紫（桃色と紫の中間色）\nルブラ 'Rubra' - 赤紫（桃色と紫の中間色）\nヨコバイ、カイガラムシ、アリマキ・キジラミ（殊にCacopsylla pulchella）といった害虫や、根こぶ病、癌腫病、バーティシリウム萎凋病などの病気に弱い。\n播種や挿し木・芽接ぎで繁殖する。\n魅力的な木目のある硬質の木材が取れる。ベニヤ板に利用され、良いつやが出る。",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cercis siliquastrum」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cercis_siliquastrum#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1360419475,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "The species prefers  deep, well-drained soils and a position in full sun or partial shade.\nCultivars include:\n\n'Afghan Deep Purple'\n'Alba' - white flowers\n'Bodnant'\n'Carnea'\n'Fructa Rubra'\n'Penduliflora'\n'Rubra' - dark pink-purple flowers\n'Sterilis'\n'Variegata'\n'White Swan'\nThe cultivar 'Bodnant' has gained the Royal Horticultural Society's Award of Garden Merit. (confirmed 2017).\nThe tree is susceptible to leafhoppers,  scale insects and psyllids (specifically Cacopsylla pulchella) as well as diseases including canker, coral spot and verticillium wilt.\nPropagation is by seed, cuttings or budding.\nThe species produces hard wood with an attractive grain. It is used in veneers and polishes well.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
